Mic input doesn't seem to work on the Soundstorm with
the latest ALSA rc. Yes, I have checked that I have
both 'CAPTURE' and 'Mic' set to full under ALSA mixer
and its not a hardware fault as it was working fine
when I was running RH9 with an earlier ALSA.

snd-intel8x0 gets listed twice during boot when it
says 'Loading ALSA Modules' (or whatever).

I'm running

ALSA driver/lib/utils 1.0.0rc2

Linux 2.4.23 w/ XFS patch

Mandrake 9.2 on a ASUS A7N8X and I'm using the onboard
sound (NFORCE2/Soundstorm).

PCM playback started working properly when I upgraded
to the latest alsa-utils, MIDI works but recording
doesn't.  This is what happens with arecord:

-----------------------------

[d@localhost d]$ arecord -l
**** List of CAPTURE Hardware Devices ****
card 0: nForce2 [NVidia nForce2], device 0: Intel ICH
[NVidia nForce2]
  Subdevices: 1/1
  Subdevice #0: subdevice #0
card 0: nForce2 [NVidia nForce2], device 1: Intel ICH
- MIC ADC [NVidia nForce2 - MIC ADC]
  Subdevices: 1/1
  Subdevice #0: subdevice #0

[d@localhost d]$ arecord -f cd -d 5 -t wav mick.wav
Recording WAVE 'mick.wav' : Signed 16 bit Little
Endian, Rate 44100 Hz, Stereo
arecord: pcm_read:1164: read error: Input/output error

